Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), libpam0g-dev, python3:native <!nocheck>
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Homepage: https://github.com/aurora-silicon/aurora-sep-userspace
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: aurora-touchid-rearm
Architecture: arm64
Depends: libpam-runtime, ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: Re-arm Touch ID with the password after a lockout
 After too many failed matches the Secure Enclave stops matching and the
 apple_sep driver refuses every verify until a password authentication, as
 macOS asks for the password. pam_aurora_touchid hands a password that the
 PAM stack has just accepted to aurora-touchid-rearm, which checks it again
 and re-arms Touch ID.
 .
 By default the first login or unlock after boot also needs the password, as
 on macOS (require_password_after_boot in /etc/aurora/touchid.conf).
